    <statement><p><p>The table shows the daily earnings, <m>e</m> Ksh, of <m>{43}</m> boda boda riders in Eldoret.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Earnings (Ksh)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{200} \le {e} \lt {400}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{400} \le {e} \lt {600}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{600} \le {e} \lt {800}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{800} \le {e} \lt {1000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1000} \le {e} \lt {1200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1200} \le {e} \lt {1400}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Use the assumed mean <m>A = {900}</m>, with <m>d = x - A</m>, where <m>x</m> is the class midpoint.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\Sigma fd</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fd =</m> <fillin characters="7" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>\Sigma fd^2</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fd^2 =</m> <fillin characters="9" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Estimate the mean, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>\bar{x} =</m> <fillin characters="7" name="ans3"/> Ksh  </div><p>(d) Estimate the standard deviation, correct to 2 decimal places. Do not round until the final answer.</p><div><m>\sigma =</m> <fillin characters="7" name="ans4"/> Ksh  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Subtracting the same number <m>A</m> from every value moves the mean down by <m>A</m> and leaves the spread unchanged. So work with <m>d = x - A</m>, where <m>x</m> is the class midpoint: add <m>A</m> back to the mean of <m>d</m>, but not to its standard deviation. Using midpoints makes these estimates.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>f</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Midpoint (<m>x</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>d = x - {900}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fd</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fd^2</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{200} \le {e} \lt {400}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{300}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-600}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1\,800\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{400} \le {e} \lt {600}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{500}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-400}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1\,280\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{600} \le {e} \lt {800}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{700}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{600\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{800} \le {e} \lt {1000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{900}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1000} \le {e} \lt {1200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1100}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{200\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1200} \le {e} \lt {1400}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1300}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{400}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1200}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{480\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Total</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{43}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-7000}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4\,360\,000}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) <m>\Sigma fd = {-7000}</m>. (b) <m>\Sigma fd^2 = {4\,360\,000}</m>.</p><p>(c) <me>\bar{x} = A + \frac{\Sigma fd}{\Sigma f} = {900} - \frac{ {7000} }{ {43} } \approx {737.2}</me></p><p>(d) <me>\sigma^2 = \frac{\Sigma fd^2}{\Sigma f} - \left(\frac{\Sigma fd}{\Sigma f}\right)^2 = \frac{ {4\,360\,000} }{ {43} } - \left(\frac{ {-7000} }{ {43} }\right)^2 \approx {74\,894.538}</me>so <m>\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2} \approx {273.67}</m> Ksh, using the unrounded variance. The variance of <m>x</m> equals the variance of <m>d</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>-7000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4360000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{31700}{43}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{200 \sqrt{3462}}{43}</m></p></answer>
